# Auto-ship (GitHub PR + GCP) — default for user-visible site work

When the user asks for site features, landing pages, or says **ship**, **push**, **PR**, or **make it live**:

## 1. Commit (scoped only)

- Stage only files for the current feature (never greenteam/diagnose/steward release binaries).
- Exclude `steward/desktop/release*/**` from every commit.
- Commit message: one line, outcome-focused.

## 2. Branch + push (GitHub)

- **Never reuse** a `cursor/*` branch after its PR merged (squash merge rewrites history).
- Fresh branch from latest production base:

  ```powershell
  git fetch origin main-fixed
  git checkout -B cursor/<feature-slug>-c7f3 origin/main-fixed
  ```

- Push: `git push -u origin HEAD`
- Open PR to **`main-fixed`** (not `master`). Merged PR link pattern: `https://github.com/codykayak/AiBhive/pull/<n>`
- **`cursor/*` PRs auto-merge** via `.github/workflows/auto-merge-cursor-prs.yml` — no manual merge needed after push.

## 3. Deploy aibhive.com (GCP)

Production is **Cloud Run `aibhive`**, not `manydoorsai`.

```powershell
cd aibhive-main-fixed
$env:OPERATOR_DIRECT='1'
npm run operator -- action submit-cloud-build --service aibhive
```

- Do this after user-visible work even if GitHub PR is still merging.
- Confirm: `npm run operator -- gcp` shows a new SUCCESS build; hard-refresh https://aibhive.com

## 4. Path hygiene (avoid “merged but 404”)

GitHub Actions deploy builds from **repo-root** `src/` and `cloudbuild.yaml`. App source in this monorepo lives under `aibhive-main-fixed/`. If a feature only lands under the nested prefix, **also mirror routes/assets into root paths on GitHub** or update root `cloudbuild.yaml` to build from `aibhive-main-fixed/`. Until then, **local operator deploy to `aibhive`** is the reliable ship path.

## 5. Do not

- Push `cursor/legal-compliance-preface-c7f3` (contains >100MB desktop release binaries).
- Default deploy to `manydoorsai` for aibhive.com work.
- Give “open PR” links for already-merged branches — link the closed PR or open a **new** branch.
